[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   TEP / Planet-9 -- step b11: population selectivity and
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   split-sample axis recovery
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   Two questions:
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   S1  Which populations carry the axis?  The detached sample
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   (a>150, q>30) carries it; do the plunging high-a objects
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   (a>150, q<=30 -- Damocloid / inner-Oort tracks that dive
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   through the inner system) show it too?  Under a boundary
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   interpretation the signature should live in the
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   boundary-resident population; plunging orbits get their
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   clock elements scrambled by the deep transit (giant-planet
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   encounters, inner-Oort tide).  Ecliptic varpi is a
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   scrambled coordinate for retrograde orbits, so the test is
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   the 3-D perihelion vector vs the axis.
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   S2  Split-sample axis recovery (the TNO-side analog of the
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   comet step_13 test): repeatedly split the detached sample
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   in half; does half B concentrate around half A's recovered
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   mean direction?  If the axis is a property of the
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   population rather than a small-N fluke, independent halves
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   should agree.
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   S3  Selectivity summary: 3-D perihelion-vector alignment with
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   the axis for every population in the catalog -- detached,
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   plunging, inner belt, Centaurs -- one table.
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   S4  Cautionary datum: the plunging sample's ecliptic varpi
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   shows an apparent R=0.22 hint at ~68 deg that VANISHES in
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   3-D -- documenting the retrograde-coordinate artifact
[2026-09-21 14:31:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 024]   explicitly.
